-- SKAI-1953 (DB-01): every campus_id that had no foreign key now references its campus, pinned to the row's own school:
-- (school_id, campus_id) -> campuses(school_id, id). A row can no longer name a missing campus or another school's.
-- NULL campus_id still means "whole school" (MATCH SIMPLE skips the check). ON DELETE NO ACTION matches the 17
-- existing pinned campus keys: campuses are only removed with their school, which cascades these rows too.
-- The app never deletes a campus on its own; if that changes, decide per table whether rows go or block it.
--
-- Keys are added NOT VALID and then validated, so existing rows are checked without blocking writes for long.
-- Indexes are plain CREATE INDEX (tables are small); for a large production table, build the index first with
-- CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY under the same name and IF NOT EXISTS skips it here.
-- Rollback: DROP CONSTRAINT "<table>_school_id_campus_id_fkey" and DROP INDEX "<table>_school_id_campus_id_idx".
SET lock_timeout = '10s';

